+
+## Billing
+
+`README.md` has the plans and the Stripe environment. In code: the plans are the `Subscription` types (`saas/app/models/subscription.rb`); `Account::Billable`, `Account::CardLimited`, and `Account::StorageLimited` are mixed into `Account` from the engine and decide the plan and its limits; `Account::Subscription` mirrors the Stripe subscription from the webhooks at `Stripe::WebhooksController`. The tenanted billing routes (`/account/subscription`) are appended to the application routes from the engine because engine route helpers drop the account slug; the untenanted ones (`/stripe/webhooks`, `/admin/accounts`) are the engine's own. Stripe is unreachable in development and test: stub `Stripe::Checkout::Session`, `Stripe::BillingPortal::Session`, and `Stripe::Subscription`, and sign webhook payloads with `Stripe::Webhook::Signature.compute_signature`.
