+## Billing
+
+Hosted Fizzy is free up to the limits of the free plan, and Stripe bills for the paid ones:
+
+| Plan       | Price     | Cards     | Storage |
+|------------|-----------|-----------|---------|
+| Free       | —         | 1,000     | 1 GB    |
+| Unlimited  | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB    |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB  |
+
+The plans are the `Subscription` types (`FreeV1`, `MonthlyV1`, `MonthlyExtraStorageV1`). Every card counts against the free plan, drafts included, and the count never goes down, since card numbers are handed out from it. A free account that runs out of cards can still draft: publishing and creating through the API are refused, the create buttons give way to an upgrade pitch, and from 100 cards out a warning counts down. Storage works the same way, with each plan bringing its own allowance.
+
+Stripe hosts Checkout and the customer portal, both reached from the account's plan page (`/account/subscription`), and posts subscription changes to `/stripe/webhooks`, which mirrors them onto `Account::Subscription`. Canceling a Fizzy account cancels its Stripe subscription. The environment needs:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` — the signing secret of the webhook endpoint, subscribed to `checkout.session.completed`, `customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`, `customer.subscription.deleted`, and `invoice.upcoming`
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` and `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` — the Stripe prices of the paid plans
+
+Support tools live in the admin area: `/admin/accounts` lists the accounts, and each account's page can comp it (the top plan for nothing), override the card count and bytes used that the limits are enforced against, or reset that override.
+
